WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.125
ArriveCAN.

00:00:01.125 --> 00:00:04.034
Original estimate: eighty thousand dollars.

00:00:04.034 --> 00:00:06.568
Final cost: ninety-three million.

00:00:06.568 --> 00:00:10.011
That is a one hundred and sixteen thousand percent overrun.

00:00:10.011 --> 00:00:11.886
For a COVID border questionnaire.

00:00:11.886 --> 00:00:14.727
One hundred and seventy-seven documented bugs.

00:00:14.727 --> 00:00:17.193
Ten thousand wrongful quarantines.

00:00:17.193 --> 00:00:21.784
Seventy-six percent of subcontractors hired performed zero work on the project.

00:00:21.784 --> 00:00:28.613
GCStrategies — a two-person firm — billed nineteen point one million dollars without writing a single line of code.

00:00:28.613 --> 00:00:33.306
Forty contract amendments approved without scrutiny during COVID emergency procurement.

00:00:33.306 --> 00:00:41.409
The Auditor General found that the Canada Border Services Agency could not document the exact cost or prove that work was completed before payment was issued.

00:00:41.409 --> 00:00:49.022
June 2025: Parliament voted one hundred and seventy-two to one hundred and sixty-five to recover sixty-four million dollars.

00:00:49.022 --> 00:00:52.113
Every single Liberal MP voted against returning the money.

00:00:52.113 --> 00:00:53.102
Every one.

00:00:53.102 --> 00:00:54.659
The vote is on the record.

00:00:54.659 --> 00:00:56.011
The money is not.
